  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Resilient Communities for Sustainable Development in Rural Afghanistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To strengthen the resilience of rural communities in Afghanistan to economic, climatic, and conflict-related shocks. The project will be implemented in underserved, rural communities across nine provinces of Afghanistan &#x2013; Badghis, Balkh, Ghazni, Herat, Maidan Wardak, Nimroz, Paktia, Zabul, and Kandahar. The project is designed to consolidate and build upon the  consortium partners&#x2019; ongoing  humanitarian and  recovery programmes through a complementary approach, in which members will mutually benefit from each other&#x2019;s skills and experience  to  generate  the  highest  positive  impact  among  affected  populations</narrative>
  </description>
